_vrf_PLAT234_jin219
;
PROBLEM: Large Hirshfeld Difference N1       --C1       .       0.17 Ang.  
RESPONSE: Unlike its neighbors, atom C1 does not bond with sp2 carbons
 like atom C2 or undergo H bonding like atom N1. The larger Ueq can
 be attributed to its larger thermal disorder.
;
_vrf_PLAT241_jin219
;
PROBLEM: High   'MainMol' Ueq as Compared to Neighbors of         I4 Check 
RESPONSE: Atom I4 is coordinated to two neighboring tin atoms that
 have lower vibrational freedom comparatively due to their coord-
 ination environments. Therefore it is not unexpected that I4 has a high
 Ueq compared to its neighbors.
;
_vrf_PLAT242_jin219
;
PROBLEM: Low    'MainMol' Ueq as Compared to Neighbors of        Sn1 Check 
RESPONSE: Atoms Sn1 and Sn2 are coordinated to six neighboring iodide atoms
 that have greater vibrational freedom comparatively. Therefore it is not
 unexpected that Sn1 has a low Ueq compared to its neighbors. Similarly,
 atom C3 is sp2 hybridized and more rigid compared to its neighbor C2.
;
_vrf_PLAT342_jin219
;
PROBLEM: Low Bond Precision on  C-C Bonds ...............    0.01588 Ang.  
RESPONSE: This is the best possible bond precision for the collected
 data.
;
_vrf_PLAT906_jin219
;
PROBLEM: Large K Value in the Analysis of Variance ......      3.555 Check 
RESPONSE: Usually data integration algorithms underestimate the background
 and produces slightly elevated values of Fo, resulting in higher Fo/Fc
 values. These are most pronounced for the weakest intensities.
;
_vrf_PLAT976_jin219
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Resid. Dens.  1.09Ang From N1      .      -0.57 eA-3  
RESPONSE: This peak is smaller than the largest min/max peak density and
 is in a chemically unreasonable position, and is therefore considered
 noise.
;
_vrf_PLAT977_jin219
;
PROBLEM: Check Negative Difference Density on H9AA      .      -0.32 eA-3  
RESPONSE: The chemical formula is known from the synthesis. All H atoms
 were placed in calculated idealized positions that are consistent with
 the hybridization of the C and N atoms. All H atoms in the model are
 needed to balance the charge.
